---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="ALL-LLLM Pod — Performance">
  <main class="performance-page">
    <a class="back" href="/projects/all-lllm-pod/">← ALL-LLLM Pod</a>

    <header class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">ALL-LLLM POD</p>
      <h1>Performance</h1>
      <p>
        Realtime voice exposed a different constraint than context-window size:
        latency.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>Realtime Metrics</h2>

      <p>
        For realtime voice, I optimized for responsiveness rather than maximum
        model quality: less prompt orchestration, fewer blocking operations, and
        TTS starting as early as possible during streaming generation.
      </p>

      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Metric</th>
            <th>Current Range</th>
            <th>Notes</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>ASR Runtime</td><td>0.16–0.29s</td><td>Whisper large-v3-turbo transcription</td></tr>
          <tr><td>MLX TTFT</td><td>0.40–0.78s</td><td>Time-to-first-token on lighter prompts</td></tr>
          <tr><td>TTFA</td><td>3.8–4.5s</td><td>Time-to-first-audio during simple conversations</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Prompt Size</td><td>1.4k–4.3k chars</td><td>Final prompt after memory and retrieval</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Memory Benchmarks</h2>

      <p>
        I replaced toy prompts with benchmarks built from the actual transcript
        corpus: roughly 75,000 speaker-labeled segments from 563 episodes, with
        controlled memory facts injected into realistic conversation history.
      </p>

      <p>
        The goal was to measure the practical cost of conversational memory:
        how much prior context could be retained before latency became
        unacceptable, and whether buried facts remained retrievable.
      </p>

      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Context</th>
            <th># Tokens</th>
            <th>p50 TTFT</th>
            <th>Equivalent</th>
            <th>Finding</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>No memory</td><td>0</td><td>0.52s</td><td>0 words</td><td>Baseline</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Short memory</td><td>~390</td><td>1.32s</td><td>~271 words / ~1.2 min</td><td>Cheap enough for realtime voice</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Moderate memory</td><td>~680</td><td>1.84s</td><td>~481 words / ~2.5 min</td><td>Still responsive</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Heavy memory</td><td>~1,940</td><td>4.50s</td><td>~1,425 words / ~6.5 min</td><td>Starts to feel heavy for voice</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Long conversation</td><td>~3,983</td><td>9.81s</td><td>~2,870 words / ~14.5 min</td><td>Latency becomes the dominant constraint</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Stress window</td><td>~7,794</td><td>22.38s</td><td>~5,670 words / ~30 min</td><td>Too slow for interactive voice</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Retrieval</h2>

      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Retrieval Test</th>
            <th>Observed Result</th>
            <th>Finding</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Explicit user memory</td><td>~100%</td><td>Clearly marked user facts were recovered reliably</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Targeted fact bank</td><td>~100%</td><td>Names, numbers, preferences, and identifiers were recovered when directly queried</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Embedded sentence</td><td>20–60%</td><td>Facts hidden inside ordinary transcript text were substantially harder to recover</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Anomaly prompt</td><td>Unstable</td><td>Measured salience more than memory</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p>
        The practical limit was not context-window capacity. It was latency and
        attention. For realtime voice, smaller sliding memory windows worked
        better; larger context was better reserved for slower text or analysis
        modes.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .performance-page {
    width: min(100% - 32px, 980px);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 48px 0 96px;
  }

  .back {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }

  .hero {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin-bottom: 64px;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    font-family: monospace;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    opacity: 0.55;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 6rem);
    line-height: 0.9;
  }

  section {
    padding: 42px 0 54px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color, #d8cdb8);
  }

  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 24px 0;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  th,
  td {
    padding: 10px 12px;
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color, #d8cdb8);
  }

  th {
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .performance-page {
      width: min(100% - 24px, 980px);
    }

    table {
      display: block;
      overflow-x: auto;
    }
  }
</style>
